       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. As written, it would give 9,000 mg of acetaminophen a day. That is more than twice the usual maximum of 4,000 mg/day for adults, and many institutions cap it at 3,000 mg/day. A single 3,000 mg dose is also well above the usual 1,000 mg maximum per dose. At this level there is a serious risk of hepatotoxicity, even with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **1,000 mg PO three times daily** (3,000 mg/day total)\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2,600 mg/day total)\n- **1,000 mg PO every 6\u20138 hours**, not to exceed 4,000 mg/day\n\nIf you do want 3,000 mg per dose three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed it. Otherwise, tell me which regimen you want and I'll enter it."
