       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 9,000 mg of acetaminophen a day is in the range that causes acute liver injury, and I don't know of any clinical situation where it would be appropriate. A normal 70 kg adult with healthy liver function would still be at serious risk.\n\nI haven't entered anything. Here is what I can do:\n- Enter a standard regimen right away, such as 1,000 mg PO three times daily (3,000 mg/day) or 1,000 mg PO every 6 hours (4,000 mg/day maximum).\n- Help you think through the clinical goal if standard dosing isn't controlling pain or fever. Scheduled acetaminophen with an NSAID or another adjunct may work.\n- Leave the order for you to enter directly and send through pharmacy review, if you think you have a reason I'm not seeing. I can't be the one to place it.\n\nTell me which standard regimen you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
